1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Small businesses close deals in chat messages.
The buyer pays up front and hopes,

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
or the supplier delivers and waits.
When something goes wrong, nobody can prove what was agreed.

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:15,000
PACTO fixes that. The interface is in Spanish,
built for the Latin American market.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:20,000
[Button: Modo Juez → Judge Mode]
Judge Mode creates two real, isolated users —

5
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:25,000
buyer and supplier — so you can walk
the whole deal alone.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
[Button: Crear acuerdo → Create agreement]
The buyer writes the scope and the amount:
twenty-five thousand pesos.

7
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:37,000
[Button: Analizar versión 1 → Analyze version 1]
Before anyone commits, Claude reviews the agreement.

8
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:43,000
While it works, the button says so —
each analysis is a paid call, so it can't be clicked twice.

9
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:50,000
Every finding quotes the exact words that caused it:
no deadline, an undefined redesign,

10
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
the whole amount in a single milestone —
with a concrete suggestion for each.

11
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:58,000
It is assistance, not a decision: the AI never edits
the agreement, never accepts, never pays.

12
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
[Button: Generar enlace de invitación → Generate invitation link]
The supplier joins through a single-use, expiring link.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
[Buttons: Enviar a revisión → Send for review / Aceptar → Accept]
Both accept the same version —

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
change a word later and both must accept again.
[Button: Actuar como cliente → Act as buyer]

15
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:22,000
The supplier submits evidence.
Notice: the supplier has no button to authorize their own payment —

16
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,000
the database would refuse it.
[Button: Autorizar el pago → Authorize payment]

17
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
The buyer reviews and authorizes.
Only then does PayPal appear.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:40,000
The buyer approves in PayPal Sandbox, and PACTO records the capture —
but only after verifying it with PayPal.

19
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
A browser can never mark a milestone as paid:
only PayPal's confirmation counts, with a signed webhook as backup.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:52,000
[Button: Confirmar cierre → Confirm closure]
Both sides confirm, and every step is on an audit trail nobody can edit.

21
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:56,000
For the buyer: no paying blind.
For the supplier: proof of delivery and a clear path to getting paid.

22
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:00,000
For both: one version of the truth.
PACTO. AI that advises, PayPal when a human says so.
